.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ckman-piv-decrypt 1  ckman 
.SH NAME
ckman\-piv\-decrypt \- Perform the raw RSA private operation on a ciphertext (the output is still padded; unpadding is the caller\*(Aqs job)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBckman\-piv\-decrypt\fR [\fB\-P\fR|\fB\-\-pin\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISLOT\fR> <\fIINPUT\fR> <\fIOUTPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Perform the raw RSA private operation on a ciphertext (the output is still padded; unpadding is the caller\*(Aqs job)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-P\fR, \fB\-\-pin\fR \fI<PIN>\fR
PIN code (prompted when needed)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISLOT\fR>
PIV slot holding an RSA key
.TP
<\fIINPUT\fR>
File containing the modulus\-sized ciphertext (\*(Aq\-\*(Aq for stdin)
.TP
<\fIOUTPUT\fR>
File to write the raw plaintext block to (\*(Aq\-\*(Aq for stdout)
